# Image generation runs in subagents

Never call `GenerateImage` directly on the main thread. Image generation is slow and
blocks everything behind it.

Delegate every image to a background subagent, then keep working.

## How

```
Task(
  subagent_type: "generalPurpose",
  run_in_background: true,
  description: "Generate <short name>",
  prompt: "<full image description>
           Save to: /absolute/path/to/output.png
           Use the GenerateImage tool. Aspect ratio: 16:9.
           Return the absolute path of the file you created."
)
```

Then continue with other work or end the turn. The completion notification arrives
on its own — do not poll with `AwaitShell`.

## Rules

- **One subagent per image** when generating a set, launched in a single message so
  they run in parallel. Do not serialize a batch through one subagent.
- **Always specify the absolute output path and filename** in the prompt. Otherwise
  the file lands somewhere unpredictable and has to be hunted down.
- **Always ask the subagent to return the absolute path** it wrote.
- **Carry the full spec into the prompt.** The subagent cannot see this conversation,
  the project bible, or any prior context. Style constraints, negative constraints,
  and resolution requirements must all be restated in the prompt text.
- **After completion, verify then display.** Read the returned path and embed it with
  `![alt](/absolute/path.png)` so the result is visible in chat.

## Project-specific

For this project, every generation prompt must also carry the standing constraints
from `bible/00-scope-and-decisions.md`: no text of any kind in the image, late-antique
376 CE material culture only, no invented ornament, and ~3× final linear resolution
with crop headroom for the intended move.
